Built without the warning flags the corpus applies to its own code, and
UBSan reports left shifts of negative values in it, at tweetnacl.c:281
and tweetnacl.c:685. Both are the reference file as published. The
policy here is that a vendored file is not edited, so they stand; they
are noted because a sanitizer build of dump will print them, and the
first reaction should not be to look for the bug in cmd/.

tweetnacl declares randombytes but does not define it. dump supplies a
definition that serves crypto_sign_keypair a caller-chosen seed, which
is how an Ed25519 public key is derived from a given private key
without editing the vendored source. dump never needs real randomness;
that definition aborts if called for any other purpose.
